      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Strongest toxic plant in the set. NC State rates severity high and says it may be fatal to pets and livestock; Clemson warns of throat swelling and suffocation. Ingestion is stored as severity 3 (our 0-3 scale: can be life-threatening); this grade was a deliberate choice. Growth 'fast' is for ideal conditions only (Clemson); size is NC State's 3-8 ft by 2-3 ft, Clemson 3-6 ft by 1-3 ft. Interval: NC State 'water thoroughly and let the top 1 inch dry completely before watering again'; Missouri Botanical Garden 'water regularly during the growing season, allow soils to dry between waterings, reduce fall to late winter'; Clemson (earlier read) agrees on drying between. Top inch dry in a 13 cm pot is about 8 days. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, growing season; winter comes from the rest-season factor. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives any, unchanged."
      },
